# Local Darwin build config. Overrides example_config.bzl when present, and
# platform/ios/bazel/macros.bzl bakes its API_KEY straight into the built app's
# Info.plist -- so this file HOLDS A REAL API KEY whenever anyone builds the
# demo app against a real gateway. Never commit it.
#
# It is also the ONLY channel that works: editing platform/ios/app/Info.plist by
# hand does nothing, because bazel regenerates the plist and runs
# `plutil -replace MLNApiKey` with API_KEY from here. A hand-edited plist builds
# fine and ships the 0000000000 placeholder, which then 401s on session create
# with no obvious cause.
#
# Copy example_config.bzl and change API_KEY only -- the other symbols
# (APPLE_MOBILE_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_NAME and friends) must survive or
# platform/ios/bazel/provisioning.bzl fails to load and the whole package stops
# resolving.
/config.bzl
